---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import olivierKeynote from '../assets/images/olivier-keynote.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Ridgeline"
  description="Readiness under pressure, for leaders and teams. The discipline that gets a team safely up a mountain — brought to how your people lead and decide when it counts."
  lang="en"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <div class="hero-in">
        <span class="badge">Now booking</span>
        <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--sky)">Leadership · keynote</div>
        <h1>Readiness under pressure. <em>For the people who lead.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          <strong>The Ridgeline</strong> is a keynote for companies and
          leadership teams — drawn from real decisions above 6,000 metres, on
          how the best prepare, stay composed, and find the courage to make
          the hard call. The same discipline that gets a team safely up a
          mountain, brought to how your people lead when it counts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-photo">
      <Image src={olivierKeynote} alt="Olivier delivering a keynote on stage" class="hero-img" width={1400} quality={78} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
      <div class="hero-seam"></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- BRIDGE -->
  <section class="bridge">
    <div class="narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Why the mountain</div>
      <h2 class="serif">The mountain is the sharpest classroom there is.</h2>
      <p>
        High-altitude objectives strip leadership down to its essentials.
        There's no room for noise: you prepare properly or you don't summit;
        you read the conditions honestly or you get hurt; you make the hard
        call — to push or to turn — when it matters, not after.
      </p>
      <p>
        The same discipline that decides an expedition decides how a team
        performs under real pressure: <strong>knowing what matters, adapting
        when reality changes, and having the composure to own the
        decision.</strong> Higher Ground brings that discipline — drawn from
        real mountains and real decisions — into the room where your people
        lead.
      </p>
      <p class="kicker">Not motivation. Not metaphor for its own sake. The same readiness, applied where the stakes are different but no less real.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOR WHOM -->
  <section class="whom">
    <svg class="contours" viewBox="0 0 1200 400" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
      <g fill="none" stroke="#7FB0D9" stroke-width="1">
        <path d="M-50,300 C260,250 400,180 600,196 C800,212 920,150 1070,158 C1175,163 1240,150 1260,154" opacity=".38"/>
        <path d="M-50,250 C280,196 420,126 620,140 C820,154 940,92 1078,98 C1180,102 1245,92 1260,96" opacity=".42"/>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <div class="wrap whom-in">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--sky)">Who it's for</div>
      <h2 class="serif">For teams that carry real consequences.</h2>
      <div class="whom-list">
        <span class="whom-item">Scale-ups navigating uncertainty</span>
        <span class="whom-item">Leadership offsites</span>
        <span class="whom-item">Executive teams under pressure</span>
        <span class="whom-item">High-stakes, high-change environments</span>
        <span class="whom-item">Teams rebuilding trust and composure</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRINCIPLES -->
  <section class="principles">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="principles-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">What it teaches</div>
        <h2 class="serif">Three lessons from the high mountains.</h2>
        <p>Each one is a mountaineering truth first, and a leadership truth second — grounded in the field, not the boardroom.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prin-grid">
        <div class="prin">
          <div class="n">01</div>
          <h4>Structure over perfection</h4>
          <p>Summits aren't won by heroic effort on the day — they're won by consistent, structured preparation over months. The same is true of teams that perform when it counts.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prin">
          <div class="n">02</div>
          <h4>Consistency over intensity</h4>
          <p>The mountain rewards the steady, not the spectacular. Sustainable output, honest pacing, and recovery beat bursts of intensity that leave you depleted at altitude — or burnt out at work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prin">
          <div class="n">03</div>
          <h4>The courage to turn around</h4>
          <p>The hardest, most important leadership decision on any mountain is knowing when <em>not</em> to go. The honesty to make that call — early, and out loud — is what keeps teams safe and credible.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OFFERINGS -->
  <section class="offerings">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="off-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">The keynote</div>
        <h2 class="serif">The Ridgeline</h2>
        <p>A talk drawn from real mountains and real decisions — and what they teach about leading when the stakes are real.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ridgeline">
        <div class="ridge-main">
          <div class="dur">≈ 45 minutes · conferences · leadership offsites · team events</div>
          <p class="lead"><strong>Most talks about resilience borrow the mountain as a metaphor. The Ridgeline is the opposite</strong> — it starts from what actually happens above 6,000 metres, where preparation, composure and honest decisions are the difference between summiting safely and getting hurt, and draws the leadership lessons out from there.</p>
          <p>It's built around three truths the high mountains make unavoidable — <strong>structure over perfection, consistency over intensity, and the courage to turn around</strong> — and translated into something a leadership team can use the moment they're back at their desks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ridge-side">
          <div class="ridge-lab">What you can expect</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Grounded in first-hand expeditions, not borrowed imagery</li>
            <li>Practical takeaways your team can act on immediately</li>
            <li>Adaptable to your event, audience and theme</li>
            <li>Delivered in English, French or Spanish</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/enquire" class="btn btn-primary">Enquire about The Ridgeline</a>
          <a href="/the-ridgeline-preview.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="preview-link">Preview the keynote ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="soon">
        <div class="soon-tag">Coming soon</div>
        <div class="soon-body">
          <h4>SUMMIT — an immersive leadership experience</h4>
          <p>A longer-form, experiential format built around a mountain ascent — decisions, trade-offs and readiness under constraint, lived rather than lectured. In development.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/enquire" class="soon-link">Register interest →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOUNDER -->
  <section class="founder">
    <div class="founder-in">
      <div class="eyebrow">Who delivers it</div>
      <h2 class="serif">Someone who has actually led in both worlds.</h2>
      <p>
        Higher Ground's leadership work is delivered by <strong>Olivier
        Gil</strong> — for over fifteen years both a senior executive in a
        high-stakes profession and a serious alpinist. This isn't a
        mountaineer theorising about business, or a consultant borrowing a
        summit photo. It's <strong>genuine dual fluency</strong>: the same
        person who has made the hard call on a mountain has made it in the
        room.
      </p>
      <a class="btn-quiet" href="/about">More about Olivier →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLOSING CTA -->
  <section class="cta">
    <div class="cta-in">
      <span class="badge">Now booking</span>
      <h2 class="serif">Bring the mountain to your team.</h2>
      <p>The Ridgeline is available now for conferences, offsites and leadership events. If you're planning a moment where readiness under pressure matters, let's talk about the date.</p>
      <a href="/enquire" class="btn btn-primary">Let's talk</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* HERO — split: solid navy text zone, photo zone with a gradient seam
     blending into it. Avoids relying on a scrim over the whole photo (which
     was fighting the stage lighting) and gives the photo room to keep the
     subject fully in frame instead of being force-cropped to fill 100% width. */
  .hero { display: flex; align-items: stretch; min-height: 560px; background: var(--navy-deep); }
  .hero-text { flex: 0 0 44%; display: flex; align-items: center; position: relative; z-index: 2; }
  .hero-in { padding: 92px 32px 92px 32px; max-width: 560px; margin-left: auto; }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sky-bright);
    border: 1px solid rgba(127,176,217,.4); border-radius: 100px; padding: 6px 14px; margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif; font-weight: 600;
    color: #fff; font-size: clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 22px;
  }
  .hero h1 em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sky-bright); }
  .hero-sub { font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.6vw, 17px); color: #C8D6E5; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.6; }
  .hero-sub strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 500; }
  .hero-photo { flex: 1; position: relative; overflow: hidden; min-width: 0; }
  .hero-photo :global(.hero-img) {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 14%; display: block;
    filter: saturate(.22) contrast(1.05) brightness(.92);
  }
  .hero-seam {
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background:
      linear-gradient(90deg, var(--navy-deep) 0%, rgba(3,13,30,.8) 10%, rgba(3,13,30,.4) 28%, rgba(3,13,30,.22) 50%, rgba(3,13,30,.22) 100%);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero { flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }
    .hero-text { flex: none; }
    .hero-in { margin: 0; max-width: none; padding: 48px 32px 36px; }
    .hero-photo { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; }
    .hero-seam { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--navy-deep) 0%, rgba(3,13,30,.55) 14%, transparent 40%); }
  }

  /* BRIDGE */
  .bridge { padding: 92px 0; }
  .bridge h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 3.6vw, 38px); color: var(--navy); line-height: 1.16; margin-bottom: 22px; max-width: 22ch; }
  .bridge p { font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .bridge p strong { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 600; }
  .kicker {
    font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(18px, 2.2vw, 22px); color: var(--navy);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--sky); padding-left: 22px; margin-top: 26px !important; line-height: 1.48;
  }

  /* PRINCIPLES */
  .principles { background: var(--ice); padding: 92px 0; }
  .principles-head { max-width: 620px; margin-bottom: 42px; }
  .principles-head h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 3.6vw, 38px); color: var(--navy); line-height: 1.16; margin-top: 12px; }
  .principles-head p { font-size: 16.5px; color: var(--text-mid); margin-top: 14px; line-height: 1.62; }
  .prin-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .prin { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 30px 28px; transition: transform .25s, box-shadow .25s; }
  .prin:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); box-shadow: 0 14px 40px -20px rgba(7,29,63,.22); }
  .prin .n { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--sky); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .prin h4 { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); letter-spacing: -.01em; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.28; }
  .prin p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.6; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .prin-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* OFFERINGS */
  .offerings { padding: 92px 0; }
  .off-head { max-width: 620px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .off-head h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 4.2vw, 46px); color: var(--navy); line-height: 1.1; margin-top: 12px; }
  .off-head p { font-size: 16.5px; color: var(--text-mid); margin-top: 14px; line-height: 1.62; }
  .ridgeline { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; background: #fff; }
  .ridge-main { padding: 42px 42px; }
  .ridge-main .dur { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--sky); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .ridge-main .lead { font-size: 17px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.68; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .ridge-main p { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.68; }
  .ridge-main strong { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 600; }
  .ridge-side { background: var(--navy-deep); color: #fff; padding: 42px 36px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .ridge-lab { font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sky); margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .ridge-side ul { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 13px; margin-bottom: 26px; flex: 1; }
  .ridge-side li { font-size: 14.5px; color: #C4D4E4; line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 20px; position: relative; }
  .ridge-side li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 8px; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--sky); }
  .preview-link {
    display: block; text-align: center; margin-top: 12px; font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--sky-bright); border: 1px solid rgba(127,176,217,.35); border-radius: 100px;
    padding: 12px 20px; transition: all .2s;
  }
  .preview-link:hover { background: rgba(127,176,217,.12); border-color: var(--sky); }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .ridgeline { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .soon {
    margin-top: 16px; border: 1px dashed var(--ice-line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 26px 30px;
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; background: var(--paper);
  }
  .soon-tag {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--steel); border: 1px solid var(--ice-line); border-radius: 100px; padding: 6px 12px; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .soon-body { flex: 1; }
  .soon-body h4 { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .soon-body p { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-lt); line-height: 1.55; }
  .soon-link {
    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace; font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sky); white-space: nowrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ice-line); padding-bottom: 3px; transition: all .2s;
  }
  .soon-link:hover { color: var(--navy); border-color: var(--navy); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .soon { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 14px; } }

  /* FOR WHOM */
  .whom { background: var(--navy-deep); color: #fff; padding: 88px 0; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .whom .contours { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; pointer-events: none; opacity: .3; }
  .whom-in { position: relative; z-index: 2; }
  .whom h2 { font-size: clamp(25px, 3.4vw, 36px); line-height: 1.18; margin: 12px 0 24px; max-width: 22ch; }
  .whom-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .whom-item { font-size: 14.5px; color: #C4D4E4; border: 1px solid rgba(127,176,217,.3); border-radius: 100px; padding: 10px 20px; }

  /* FOUNDER */
  .founder { padding: 84px 0; background: var(--ice); }
  .founder-in { max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center; padding: 0 32px; }
  .founder h2 { font-size: clamp(22px, 2.9vw, 30px); color: var(--navy); margin: 12px 0 18px; line-height: 1.25; }
  .founder p { font-size: 16.5px; color: var(--text-mid); line-height: 1.68; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .founder p strong { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 600; }

  /* CTA */
  .cta { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; padding: 90px 0; }
  .cta .badge { color: var(--sky-bright); border-color: rgba(127,176,217,.4); }
  .cta-in { text-align: center; max-width: 620px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px; }
  .cta h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .cta p { color: #B8CBDE; font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.62; margin-bottom: 30px; }
</style>
